{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q27888207","formula":"C₂₆H₃₀BrNO₄S₂","hill":"C26H30BrNO4S2","elements":["H","C","N","O","S","Br"],"composition":{"C":26.0,"H":30.0,"N":1.0,"O":4.0,"S":2.0,"Br":1.0},"names":{"en":"Aclidinium bromide"},"descriptions":{"en":"Aclidinium bromide (INN) is a long-acting, inhaled muscarinic antagonist (LAMA) approved in the United States in July 2012 as a maintenance treatment for chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). Evidence shows that it can improve quality of life and prevent hospitalization in those with COPD. However, it does not appear to affect the risk of death or the frequency steroids are needed. It is unclear if it differs from the similar medication tiotropium or other commonly used medications from the class of LAMAs."},"fame":15,"pubchemCid":11519741,"mass":564.6,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1C[N+]2(CCC1[C@H](C2)OC(=O)C(C3=CC=CS3)(C4=CC=CS4)O)CCCOC5=CC=CC=C5.[Br-]","inchikey":"XLAKJQPTOJHYDR-QTQXQZBYSA-M","iupac":"[(3R)-1-(3-phenoxypropyl)-1-azoniabicyclo[2.2.2]octan-3-yl] 2-hydroxy-2,2-dithiophen-2-ylacetate bromide","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"11519741","atoms":64,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-0.95,"y":1.183,"z":1.7,"el":"C"},{"x":0.023,"y":1.04,"z":0.53,"el":"C"},{"x":0.792,"y":-0.292,"z":0.664,"el":"N"},{"x":1.416,"y":-0.396,"z":2.064,"el":"C"},{"x":0.305,"y":-0.423,"z":3.117,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.059,"y":-0.133,"z":2.481,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.4,"y":-1.28,"z":1.513,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.241,"y":-1.458,"z":0.505,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.634,"y":-0.941,"z":0.853,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.213,"y":-1.947,"z":0.13,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.643,"y":-3.022,"z":-0.06,"el":"O"},{"x":-4.594,"y":-1.577,"z":-0.471,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.473,"y":-0.912,"z":-1.836,"el":"C"},{"x":-5.466,"y":-0.8,"z":-2.8,"el":"C"},{"x":-5.036,"y":-0